    rdf:value """Thursday, Oct. 4, 1906
Very warm and sunny
I Tatti
A marvellous day for happiness. I passed it quite alone, Bernhard being with the Lamberts all day. Ray wrote me a wonderful Full Moon letter, saying she had had a revelation of the Joy of Life.
They call Mme Lambert “Lucia Gallopaia”. Mrs. Gardner arrived at 4, and seemed as enchanting and adorable as ever!
Friday, Oct. 5, 1906
Fine
I Tatti
Mrs. Gardner.
Went to Pitti. Mrs. G.[ardner] took a hatred to Mme Lambert, because B.B. is devoted to her.
The Ripleys came to tea. She is very bad form but the daughter nice.
M. Lambert and Mme
Saturday, Oct. 6, 1906
Fine.
Sunday, Oct. 7, 1906
Fine."""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 123 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1906> .

